## Test Naming Convention

<% if (language === 'java') { %>
| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Unit test | `*Test.java` | `OrderServiceTest.java` |
| Integration test | `*IT.java` | `OrderRepositoryIT.java` |
| Architecture test | `*ArchTest.java` | `DependencyFlowArchTest.java` |

Method names: `given_<context>_when_<action>_then_<expected>` or use `@DisplayName`.
<% } else if (language === 'typescript') { %>
| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Unit / integration | `*.test.ts` | `orderService.test.ts` |
| E2E / component | `*.spec.ts` | `checkout.spec.ts` |

Describe blocks: outer = subject, inner = context (`given X`). `it()` = behaviour (`when Y then Z`).
<% } else if (language === 'rust') { %>
| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Unit (inline) | `mod tests { }` inside `src/` | — |
| Integration | `*_test.rs` in `tests/` | `order_service_test.rs` |

Function names: `given_<context>_when_<action>_then_<expected>`.
<% } else if (language === 'go') { %>
| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| All tests | `*_test.go` | `order_service_test.go` |

Use `t.Run("given X / when Y / then Z", ...)` for behavioural subtests.
<% } else if (language === 'python') { %>
| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Test file | `test_*.py` | `test_order_service.py` |
| Test class | `class Test<Subject>` | `class TestOrderService` |
| Test method | `def test_<behaviour>` | `def test_when_empty_returns_zero` |
<% } %>

